sections.example:
Tool: search_lessons
Input: {"query": nonblank string, maximum 80 characters}
Output: {"hits": [{"id": string, "title": string, "excerpt": string}]}
Effects: reads an approved local collection only
Failure: invalid query, unavailable source, malformed upstream result
Empty hits: successful lookup with no matching evidence

def validate_query(args):
    if type(args) is not dict or set(args) != {"query"}:
        raise ValueError("expected query only")
    q = args["query"]
    if type(q) is not str or len(q) > 80 or not q.strip():
        raise ValueError("query must be 1..80 characters")
    return q.strip()
assert validate_query({"query": " joins "}) == "joins"

Expected: {"hits": [{"id": "SQL-07", "title": "Joins", "excerpt": "..."}]}
Reject:   {"hits": "everything is fine"}
Reject:   two records with the same ID and conflicting content
Bound:    at most 3 hits; at most 300 characters per excerpt
Record:   source collection and revision when available
